  lessonID: 13
  cocID: COC_02
  lessonTitle: Disposing Excess Components
  description: 
  lessonSceneName: LessonScene
  requiredGoldLessonID: 12
  learningObjectives:
  - "\u2022 Identify ways of disposing excess components and materials used in networking "
  - "\u2022 Follow proper ways of segregation of disposal  "
  subtopics: []
  slides:
  - subtopicID: 1301
    slideType: 0
    content: "Proper Ways of Copper Cable Disposal \r\n\r\n1.) Keep/Store in box
      or any storage and not in a garbage bin.  \r\n2.) Bundle your copper wire to
      make it manageable to handle, and weigh it. It is useful to have an estimate
      of how much copper you have so you can discuss price and transportation with
      the recycling company. \r\n3.) Find a scrap metal company online or in your
      local phone book. Copper recycling is a very common thing in the scrap metal
      world, and recyclers make money by selling the scrap to smelting companies.
      \r\n4.) Call a few local companies and ask about prices and transportation.
      Some companies only deal in very large amounts of copper, such as leftovers
      from a building site, but others will take any weight. \r\n5.) Tell the scrap
      metal representative if you have insulated copper wire. Depending on the type
      of insulation, the recycler must either burn off the insulation or use a mechanical
      process and bury the waste if burning will produce pollutants. \r\n6.) Follow
      the scrap metal company's instructions for transport of the wire, whether it
      means dropping it off or placing it outside for collection. "
